# Tusk application

## Database changes

Create an entity, generate and review its migration, then check and apply versions:

```bash
php vendor/bin/tusk make:entity Billing/Invoice
php vendor/bin/tusk make:migration "Create invoices"
php vendor/bin/tusk migrate:status
php vendor/bin/tusk migrate --dry-run
php vendor/bin/tusk migrate
```

Production deployments must explicitly acknowledge schema changes with
`php vendor/bin/tusk migrate --allow-production`. To export SQL for review, use
`php vendor/bin/tusk migrate --write-sql=var/migrations.sql`. Rollbacks require
an explicit target and `--allow-down`; production additionally requires
`--allow-production`. `schema:sync --force` is a local development convenience
and is prohibited in production. Existing databases are never baselined
automatically; back them up, compare the schema, and explicitly register a
reviewed baseline migration before applying later versions.

See the [database migrations guide](https://github.com/tusk-framework/tusk-framework/blob/main/docs/database-migrations.md)
for the complete workflow and safeguards.
